CORE broken-cprover-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
memcpy with a symbolic size into a struct and into a union, starting partway
into a member. Byte-operator lowering used to keep the wrong original bytes
of the target past the end of the update.
With or without the fix, CPROVER SMT2 reports VERIFICATION ERROR and the
new SMT back-end fails an invariant (unimplemented conversion of a tuple
expression), hence broken-cprover-smt-backend and no-new-smt.
